---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Sidebar from '../components/Sidebar.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About John Doe and the Breath digital garden theme.">
  <Sidebar />

  <main class="site-content">
    <h2 class="page-title">about</h2>
    <p class="page-desc">Engineer, tinkerer, and systems thinker.</p>

    <div class="about-prose prose">
      <p>
        Hi, I'm <strong>John Doe</strong>. I build scalable backend systems, distributed architectures, and developer tools.
      </p>

      <p>
        This website is built with <strong>Breath</strong>, a minimalist digital garden and engineering blog theme for <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a>. It blends traditional long-form essays with an evolving, interlinked knowledge garden.
      </p>

      <h3>Philosophy</h3>
      <p>
        I believe in deep modules, ruthless simplification, and tending thoughts over time. Writing is the highest-leverage way to refine mental models and share learnings with the engineering community.
      </p>

      <h3>Stack & Colophon</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Framework:</strong> Astro 5+ (zero client framework overhead)</li>
        <li><strong>Typography:</strong> Yanone Kaffeesatz & JetBrains Mono</li>
        <li><strong>Styling:</strong> Pure CSS variables, responsive drawers, strict dark/light contrast</li>
        <li><strong>Knowledge Graph:</strong> Bi-directional wikilinks & Andy Matuschak-style stacked note previews</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Get in Touch</h3>
      <p>
        Find me on <a href="https://github.com/netologist/breath" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> or reach out via <a href="mailto:john.doe@example.com">email</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    margin-bottom: 0.35em;
  }
</style>
